# Local configuration of the Research Studio. Copy this file to .env (ignored by git) and edit it.
# Nothing here is required: without a .env the Studio uses the local Ollama with qwen3:4b.
# Restart start_studio.bat after changing it. Never commit .env.

# ---- Language model --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# local (default) = Ollama on this computer; ollama = an Ollama server elsewhere; openai = an OpenAI-compatible API
# WEBRAG_LLM_PROVIDER=local
# WEBRAG_LLM_MODEL=qwen3:4b

# Example: an OpenAI-compatible API (placeholders, not real values)
# WEBRAG_LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# WEBRAG_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/v1
# WEBRAG_LLM_MODEL=model-name
# WEBRAG_LLM_API_KEY=replace-with-your-key
# WEBRAG_LLM_JSON_MODE=schema
# WEBRAG_LLM_VERIFIER_MODEL=
# WEBRAG_LLM_TIMEOUT=180
#
# WEBRAG_LLM_JSON_MODE: schema | object | none (use object if the service rejects JSON schemas).
# WEBRAG_LLM_VERIFIER_MODEL: optional separate model for the verifier, on the same service.

# ---- Verification options (optional) ---------------------------------------------------------
# WEBRAG_VERIFIER=arm_c_studio
# WEBRAG_INJECTION_GUARD=exclude
# WEBRAG_QUOTE_ATTESTATION=1
#
# WEBRAG_VERIFIER: arm_c_studio (default) | arm_c | arm_c0 | quote_stance | quote_stance_ranked |
#   quote_stance_adjudicated | frozen_b.
#   arm_c_studio: Arm C agentic verification, Studio-adapted variant. It runs the frozen code and settings of the
#     agentic verification study's arm C: one verifier pass; conflicting evidence goes to an adjudicator; when no
#     passage took a side, a planner searches this run's evidence (at most 2 searches) first. Its one difference from
#     the historical method: an adjudicator decision with no passage for or against the claim is not accepted.
#   arm_c: the historical Arm C exactly (also accepts those decisions). arm_c0: historical arm C0 (no planner/search).
#   quote_stance: the previous default (legacy fallback); conflicting evidence stays INSUFFICIENT.
#   quote_stance_ranked / quote_stance_adjudicated: alternatives that are not Arm C.
#   Historical result (SciFact DEV, 188 previously used claims): Arm C macro-F1 0.7551 against 0.7153 for the rank
#   baseline, not significant (p = 0.081), with more false support (13/64 against 10/64). The Studio's accuracy with
#   Arm C has not been evaluated. Choose quote_stance when a wrongly confirmed claim is costlier than an undecided one.
# WEBRAG_INJECTION_GUARD: exclude (default: withhold instruction-like retrieved passages from every model call) |
#   flag (record them only) | off. The screen matches fixed patterns and misses paraphrased attacks.
# WEBRAG_QUOTE_ATTESTATION: on by default whenever the verifier quotes (all Arm C and quote_stance modes); records
#   where each verifier quote occurs in its passage and never changes a verdict. 0 turns it off. Asking for it with a
#   verifier that does not quote (frozen_b) stops the start with an error.
# A command-line flag of python -m webrag.server wins over these settings; an invalid value stops the Studio.

# ---- Search providers (optional) -------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENALEX_API_KEY=
# WEBRAG_CONTACT=you@example.com
# SEARXNG_URL=
# BRAVE_API_KEY=
#
# OPENALEX_API_KEY: free key; avoids the shared anonymous daily budget.
# WEBRAG_CONTACT: contact address sent with requests to the search services.
# SEARXNG_URL: your own SearXNG instance. BRAVE_API_KEY: Brave Search API (paid).

# ---- Retrieval models ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WEBRAG_MODEL_DOWNLOADS=auto
# auto: download the two retrieval models once if they are missing; 0 = never; 1 = allow.
